AMBER14SB protein (Maier, J. A. et al. JCTC 11, 3696–3713, 2015)

********************************************************************

Phosphorylated amino acids
--------------------------
The supplemental S1P/SEP, T1P/TPO and Y1P/PTR residues and bonded
parameters are generated from AmberTools phosaa14SB.lib and
frcmod.phosaa14SB. Cite Homeyer, N. et al., J. Mol. Model. 12,
281-289 (2006). The AmberTools force-field files under dat/leap are
distributed as public-domain data. The generated GROMACS port keeps
phosphate-specific atom types isolated from the base force field.
* Amber ff14SB port, converted and validated by                    *
* Vedran Miletic, Milosz Wieczor, Markus Rampp, Carsten Kutzner,   *
* Bert L. de Groot, and Vytautas Gapsys.                           *
*                                                                  *
* The publication covering the original ff14SB is                  *
* Maier, J. A. et al. ff14SB: Improving the Accuracy of Protein    *
* Side Chain and Backbone Parameters from ff99SB. J. Chem. Theory  *
* Comput. 11, 3696–3713 (2015). doi:10.1021/acs.jctc.5b00255       *
*                                                                  *
* This port follows the official AMBER14SB support distributed     *
* with GROMACS 2026. Cite the GROMACS version used and the          *
* original ff14SB publication above.                               *
********************************************************************
